--- reading it against the requirements ---------------------------------------------------------
FR-027 (the console says which slot was chosen): MET. Every boot prints "OTA: booting slot A, 2 attempts
  left" (here, and in every capture in this directory), and the kernel command line names the root.
Rolled back vs normal (US5 scenario 3): MET. After the retirement of A, `rauc status` shows the other
  slot as `bad` where a normal device shows both `good`, and `--detailed` says what had been installed
  there (fb19ed4-hang). It does not say WHY; the hung slot wrote no record (contracts/boot-interface.md).
FR-026 / SC-005 (one command: booted slot, both versions, both healths, pending confirmation): MET ONLY
  PARTLY, and only by `rauc status --detailed`, not by the `rauc status` the contract and the README named.
  1. Versions are in `--detailed` only. Plain `rauc status` prints the booted slot and the health of
     both slots and no version at all.
  2. The version is the one RAUC recorded when it last wrote the slot, which is the truth for any slot
     an update has written. A card that has only been flashed has no record for slot A, so its version
     would be missing exactly when someone first asks; this capture does not show that case.
  3. "Pending confirmation" is not stated anywhere. It can be inferred: "Activated" names a different
     slot from "Booted from" (B above: installed, not yet run). Nothing says "waiting to be confirmed".
  4. `boot status: good` does not mean confirmed. In B the new slot A is `good` before it has ever
     booted, because RAUC's U-Boot backend calls a slot good while it has attempts left. A slot that
     has booted but not yet confirmed (BOOT_A_LEFT=2) is `good` too. Only the counter, and the
     S99ota-health line, tell confirmed from merely eligible.
Also seen: a slot retired by exhausting its attempts stays in BOOT_ORDER with BOOT_<slot>_LEFT=0 and
  U-Boot skips it (A above). A slot that RAUC itself marks bad when an install starts is removed from
  BOOT_ORDER (T030). The contract had said the first of these was "absent from BOOT_ORDER"; corrected.
The genuine control of T037 is closed by section B and C: it installed, booted, confirmed itself and
  reports VERSION=6d5dbc6.
